From: arusiasotto <4206983+arusiasotto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: WoW bisect — signal_arm64 CONTEXT zeroing.

World of Warcraft Forever (WowB-ARM64.exe) is ARM64EC. Wine's PE syscall stubs and
KeServiceDescriptorTable wiring must match deck-verified TEB/KSDT dispatch; manually
mapped ntdll views need dispatcher init and NLS section fallback when maps fail.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
index c8ebcae44d5..54ff62d70e8 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
@@ -806,6 +806,7 @@ static void setup_exception( ucontext_t *sigcontext, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec )
 {
     CONTEXT context;
 
+    memset( &context, 0, sizeof(context) );
     rec->ExceptionAddress = (void *)PC_sig(sigcontext);
     save_context( &context, sigcontext );
     setup_raise_exception( sigcontext, rec, &context );
@@ -1209,6 +1210,7 @@ static void trap_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *sigcontext )
     CONTEXT ctx;
 
     rec.ExceptionAddress = (void *)PC_sig(context);
+    memset( &ctx, 0, sizeof(ctx) );
     save_context( &ctx, sigcontext );
 
     switch (siginfo->si_code)
